  "strategy": "### Approach and rationale\nThe approach leverages iterative adjustments to minimize the maximum overlap by focusing on the most contributing shift. Starting from a known initial solution, we adjust values in regions of high overlap while maintaining feasibility constraints.\n\n### Mathematical specification\nThe optimization targets minimizing \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\int h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx \\). Each adjustment ensures \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\) and \\( \\sum h = 21 \\).\n\n### Implementation procedure\n1. Initialize `h` from `initial_h_values`.\n2. Compute baseline `C_5` using cross-correlation.\n3. Iteratively:\n   a. Identify the shift \\( l \\) with maximum overlap.\n   b. Adjust `h` to reduce this maximum contribution.\n4. Track and return the best solution.\n\n### Search choices and useful variations\nStart with the initial solution and adjust in regions causing highest overlap, using a fixed step size for transfer adjustments.\n\n### Compute budget and robustness\nThe algorithm balances performance through iterative adjustments, ensuring feasibility and convergence within the time budget.\n\n### Validation and return contract\nCheck constraints and compute `C_5` to ensure a valid, improved solution is returned.",
